---
title: "One daily care task as caregivers complete it"
---
stateDiagram-v2
  state "Legend" as legend {
    lg0: open
    lg1: Breaks CompletedNeverReappears or CompletesTheOccurrenceShown or NeverCompletedTwice or NoOccurrenceSkipped
    lg2: Path to the CompletedNeverReappears or CompletesTheOccurrenceShown or NeverCompletedTwice or NoOccurrenceSkipped bug
  }
  class lg0 blue
  class lg1 breaks
  class lg2 bugPath
  s0: Due day 0, today is day 0 (nothing done yet)
  s1: Due day 0, today is day 1 (nothing done yet)
  s2: Due day 2, today is day 0 (done: day 1)
  s3: Due day 1, today is day 0 (done: day 0)
  s4: Due day 1, today is day 1 (done: day 0)
  s5: Due day 1, today is day 0 (done: day 0, day 0)
  s6: Due day 0, today is day 0 (done: day 0)
  [*] --> s0
  s0 --> s1: a new day begins
  s0 --> s0: the reminder for day 0 arrives or a caregiver picks day 1 in the calendar and taps Complete or a caregiver taps Complete in the task list for day 0 or a caregiver opens Edit Task (date shows day 0) or a caregiver tells Whiskers it was done on day 0#59; Whiskers asks to confirm
  s1 --> s1: the reminder for day 1 arrives
  s0 --> s2: the calendar's Complete saves a completion for day 1
  s0 --> s3: Complete on the reminder saves a completion for day 0 or the task list's Complete (row or sheet) saves a completion for day 0
  s1 --> s4: Complete on the reminder saves a completion for day 0
  s3 --> s6: the caregiver saves Edit Task
  s3 --> s5: Whiskers' confirmation saves a completion for day 0
  classDef breaks fill:#ffecee,stroke:#e72e3b,stroke-width:2.5px,color:#cd2834
  class s0 blue
  class s0 bugPath
  class s1 blue
  class s1 bugPath
